/-!
# Fpqc descent for the relative Hom functor: the sheaf property and descent along a covering
of the source

In the standing data of Stacks 08JT — a morphism `f : X ⟶ base` of algebraic spaces over a
scheme `S` and two quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-modules `F`, `G` — the relative Hom functor
`Hom(F, G) : (Sch/base)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Sets` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Quot/RelativeHom.lean` sends a test scheme `T` over the base to
`Hom_{𝒪_{X_T}}(F_T, G_T)`.  This file proves the two descent statements about it:

* **Stacks 08JV**, that `Hom(F, G)` satisfies the sheaf property for the fpqc topology: for an
  fpqc covering `{T_i ⟶ T}` of test schemes, a family of homomorphisms `u_i : F_{T_i} ⟶ G_{T_i}`
  whose restrictions agree on the overlaps `X_{T_i} ×_{X_T} X_{T_j} = X_{T_i ×_T T_j}` comes
  from a unique `u : F_T ⟶ G_T`;
* **Stacks 08K3**, the corresponding statement for a covering of the *source*: given an fppf
  covering `{X_i ⟶ X}` and fppf coverings `{X_{ijk} ⟶ X_i ×_X X_j}` of the overlaps, the
  diagram `Hom(F, G)(T) → ∏_i Hom(F_i, G_i)(T) ⇉ ∏_{ijk} Hom(F_{ijk}, G_{ijk})(T)` presents the
  first arrow as the equalizer of the other two, for every test scheme `T`.

Both are the same two inputs applied to different coverings: the base change of the covering is
again an fpqc covering (**Stacks 03MR**, part (3), and **Stacks 03Y9**), and homomorphisms of
quasi-coherent modules descend along an fpqc covering of algebraic spaces (**Stacks 04W8**).

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictPullbackHom`: the restriction of a homomorphism of inverse
  images along a further morphism, which is how every local homomorphism below is compared with
  its neighbours.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RestrictionsAgree`: the overlap condition on a family of local
  homomorphisms — the equalizer condition of the two tags.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HomSituation.TripleRestrictionsAgree`: the same condition read on the
  chosen coverings of the overlaps, which is the form Stacks 08K3 states it in.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.GluesModuleHomAlongFpqcCovering`: the gluing half of the
  full-faithfulness clause of Stacks 04W8, in the form both tags consume; see the
  implementation notes.  It is a theorem,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.existsUnique_restrictPullbackHom_eq_of_isFpqcCovering`.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.Functor.map_eq_of_conjHom_eq`: conjugation by a comparison is injective, so
  an equality of restrictions is an equality of inverse images.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictPullbackHom_comp`: restriction is functorial.  This is the
  associativity coherence of Stacks 03LU and carries no hypothesis.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.eq_of_restrictPullbackHom_eq_of_isFpqcCovering`: a homomorphism of
  inverse images is determined by its restrictions along an fpqc covering.  This is the
  *faithfulness* half of Stacks 04W8, which is available in this development.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictionsAgree_of_refinement`: the overlap condition may be
  checked on an fpqc covering of each overlap rather than on the overlap itself.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictPullbackHom_eq_restrictForm_of_comp_eq`: the restriction of
  a homomorphism of inverse images is the restricted reading of
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/Descent/QuasiCoherent/FpqcChartFullness.lean`; the two
  are built from the same comparison of Stacks 03LU.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.existsUnique_restrictPullbackHom_eq_of_isFpqcCovering`: **the gluing
  half of Stacks 04W8** in the form of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.GluesModuleHomAlongFpqcCovering`, with no hypothesis.  Aliased under
  that predicate's own name as `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.gluesModuleHomAlongFpqcCovering` in
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Quot/RelativeHomFpqcGluing.lean`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HomSituation.existsUnique_homMap_of_restrictionsAgree`:
  **Stacks 08JV**, elementwise, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HomSituation.isSheafFor_homFunctor`: **Stacks 08JV** as
  `CategoryTheory.Presieve.IsSheafFor` for the presieve generated by the covering family, which
  is the form the sheaf property of Stacks 08K8 consumes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HomSituation.overlapTestComparison`: the fibre product of two base
  changes of test schemes maps to the base change of their overlap, which is what carries the
  compatibility of a family of sections to the overlaps of the base changes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HomSituation.restrictionsAgree_of_tripleRestrictionsAgree`: the
  overlap condition of Stacks 08K3 implies the condition on the overlaps themselves.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HomSituation.tripleRestrictionsAgree_restrict` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HomSituation.existsUnique_sourceHom_of_tripleRestrictionsAgree`:
  **Stacks 08K3**, the two halves of the exactness of the displayed diagram — the first arrow
  lands in the equalizer of the other two, and it is a bijection onto that equalizer.

## Implementation notes

**The sheaf property is stated for a covering family, in two equivalent forms.**  There is no
fpqc topology on the test schemes over an algebraic space in this development — the same
situation as for Stacks 08K8 in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Quot/RelativeIsom.lean` — so
"satisfies the sheaf property for the fpqc topology" is read for an arbitrary fpqc covering
family of test schemes.  Elementwise that is: a family of sections agreeing on the overlaps has
a unique amalgamation, where the overlap of `T_i` and `T_j` enters through the algebraic space
`X_{T_i} ×_{X_T} X_{T_j}`, which is the base change `X_{T_i ×_T T_j}` of the overlap of the two
test schemes, and that is how the source's own proof reads the condition.  The second form is
`CategoryTheory.Presieve.IsSheafFor` for the presieve generated by the family, which is the
predicate the library already uses for the sheaf property of the relative Isom functor of
Stacks 08K8; passing from the first to the second is the only place where the overlap of two
test schemes has to be built as a test scheme, which it is, the big fppf site having fibre
products.

**Stacks 04W8 is applied through a named predicate, and the step the proofs do is not it.**
The full-faithfulness clause of Stacks 04W8 — fpqc descent of morphisms of quasi-coherent
modules on algebraic spaces — enters in two shapes.  Its faithfulness half is used directly, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasiCoherentDescent.modulePullback_map_injective_of_isFpqcCovering`.
Its gluing half is named `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.GluesModuleHomAlongFpqcCovering`: a statement
about two quasi-coherent modules on one algebraic space and one fpqc covering of it, with no
test schemes, no relative Hom functor and no sheaf condition in it.  Its two modules are
presented as inverse images `w^*F`, `w^*G` along a morphism `w` and its local Hom sets along the
composites `q i`, because that is how a base change of the standing data presents them; up to
the canonical comparisons of Stacks 03LU it is the gluing half of Stacks 04W8 and nothing more.
It is proved here, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.existsUnique_restrictPullbackHom_eq_of_isFpqcCovering`, from the
fullness half `…exists_modulePullback_map_eq_of_isFpqcCovering` at `…reprFpqcHomSurjective`.

What the proofs do is produce the covering that the descent is applied to.  For Stacks 08JV
that is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFpqcCovering_baseChangeMap`, Stacks 03MR part (3) at the base
changes of a covering family of test schemes.  For Stacks 08K3 it is the base change of the
given fppf coverings along `X_T ⟶ X`, together with the reduction of the overlap condition from
the chosen fibre products `X_{i,T} ×_{X_T} X_{j,T}` to the given refinements `X_{ijk}`, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictionsAgree_of_refinement` and the faithfulness half of
Stacks 04W8.

**Quasi-coherence of the base-changed modules is supplied from the situation.**  It is
Stacks 03GA, proved along an arbitrary morphism of algebraic spaces by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_modulePullback_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ModulePullbackQuasicoherentFromChartDiagrams.lean`, and
the quasi-coherence of the two modules on `X` it consumes is a *field* of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HomSituation`, so the two descent statements below need no further
input.  The intermediate lemmas about an arbitrary morphism `w : W ⟶ X` still take the
quasi-coherence of `w^*F` and `w^*G`, there being no situation there to read it from.

**Stacks 08K3 is stated without forming the situations of the members.**  The source writes
`Hom(F_i, G_i)(T)` for the value at `T` of the relative Hom functor of the situation
`X_i ⟶ base` with the two modules pulled back.  That set is
`Hom_{𝒪_{X_{i,T}}}(F_{i,T}, G_{i,T})`, and `X_{i,T} = X_i ×_{base} T` is the fibre product
`X_i ×_X X_T` of the member with the base change of the source; the statement below uses that
presentation, with the two modules pulled back along the composite `X_{i,T} ⟶ X_i ⟶ X`.  No
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HomSituation` for the members is formed, which would need the
quasi-coherence of the pullbacks of Stacks 03GA for each member and would add nothing: the sets
and the two parallel arrows are the same.

